// features/parent/tipsLibrary.mjs — Lumi's library: practical, age-right ideas for families
// helping a child with English at home. Pure data, read by features/parent/tips.js.
//
// Every tip is written for the ages it suits, so a parent of a 6-year-old never reads "revise
// the grammar table" and a parent of a 13-year-old never reads "sing the alphabet song".
//
//   tiers    which ages it suits: E = 5-7 (Pre-Junior), J = 7-9 (Junior A/B),
//            M = 9-11 (A, B), S = 11-13 (C, D)
//   cat      the shelf it sits on (CATEGORIES)
//   signals  what makes Lumi offer it first: skills and habits from the teacher's public notes
//            (ids from features/noteLexicon.mjs) and grade signals ('lowTest', 'lowDictation')
//   when     moments it fits: test (one coming), result (one just back), absence, homework, stars, start (Sep-Oct), xmas (Dec),
//            spring (Mar-Apr), exams (May-Jun), summer (Jul-Aug), holiday, newMonth
//   en / el  [title, why it works, one thing to try]
//
// Grounded in what works for young language learners: little-and-often practice, retrieval
// and spacing, reading aloud and shared books, songs and play for the youngest, praise for
// effort (growth mindset), warm low-pressure home talk, and parents as models, not testers.

